This message deliberately reuses the Message-ID of
plain-text-simple.eml, with a different body and a four-second later
Date. Servers do deliver the same Message-ID twice -- a Bcc to oneself, a
mailing list echo, a resend from a broken client -- so deduplication
must key on more than the Message-ID alone, and threading must not build
a cycle out of the pair.
